  "summary": "Nick Xenophon Team senator Skye Kakoschke-Moore announced her resignation from the Australian Senate after discovering she holds dual British citizenship through her mother. Her mother, born in Singapore in 1957 when it was a British colony, acquired 'citizenship of the United Kingdom and colonies,' which was formally recognized under the British Nationality Act in 1983. Kakoschke-Moore, born in Darwin in 1985, inherited this citizenship by descent. She expressed shock at the discovery, as she had previously believed she was not a British citizen based on advice given to her father when she was 12. She intends to refer the matter to the high court to determine how her Senate vacancy will be filled and expressed hope to return to the Senate in the future. A recount of the 2016 election would likely result in NXT candidate Tim Storrer taking the seat, though the party's preliminary legal advice suggests the situation may involve complex legal questions, particularly given a recent high court ruling involving Hollie Hughes."
}
```

